UPDATE cjams.progressnote
SET progressnotetypeid='786495b2-c779-4cc4-b812-6a8439bfa96e', title=NULL, description='<p><strong>Clinical Supervision:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Worker and supervisor went to Ms. Murray''s home on 7/2 to discuss long-term planning for their children. Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe both admitted to still using cocaine.</p></li><li><p>Supervisor informed them they have to complete intakes for substance use treatment and be compliant with treatment for at least 90 days in order to transition the children back to them.</p></li><li><p>Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe stated they would schedule appointments. They then told worker they both had appointments scheduled for 7/7 at 1pm. Worker asked them to sign releases for the Department to get records.</p></li><li><p>Worker reached out on 7/8 to discuss how the appointments went. No response was given. </p></li><li><p>Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe are still not responding to worker.</p></li><li><p>Ms. Murray (maternal aunt) stated she cannot keep the baby past a month or two. Concerns about finances and ability to care for a baby given her work schedule. DSS is helping with childcare for July.</p></li><li><p>Mr. Murray fine with keeping the two. DSS ordered bedding.</p></li><li><p>FIA benefits were cut off for Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe so family could apply for benefits for the children.</p></li><li><p>Complete FTDM and family find referral.</p></li></ul><p><strong>UPDATE AS OF 7/14:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Ms. Murray (maternal aunt) stated she can only keep the baby for another week or two. She rescinded her custody paperwork.</p></li><li><p>Reach out to Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe about another plan or respite.</p></li></ul>', entitytype='servicecase', entitytypeid='a005cdd3-55ac-4957-96a6-f3db60e87ad1', pagetitle=NULL, pageurl=NULL, islatest=NULL, versionof=NULL, insertedby='857bc591-61f8-4ca8-9d20-7aa3b22cc3d8', insertedon='2025-07-14 09:33:57.590', archivedby=NULL, archivedon=NULL, updatedby='857bc591-61f8-4ca8-9d20-7aa3b22cc3d8', updatedon='2