UPDATE cjams.progressnote
SET progressnotetypeid='786495b2-c779-4cc4-b812-6a8439bfa96e', title=NULL, description='<p>This worker (M. Griffin) visited the home of Amber Murray to conduct a weekly visit as requested by K. Price. Worker arrived at the home at approximately 10AM. Worker approached the apartment 106, knocked and was invited into the home by Julia Hoppe. Ms. Hoppe greeted worker as worker stepped inside the home, the home was clean. Ms. Murray was sitting in a recliner holding Joseph in her arms. Joseph appeared to be clean and in good health. Joseph was asleep, dressed in a long sleeve one piece and swaddled in a fleece blanket. Ms. Murray told worker Joseph had just drank a bottle and fell asleep. Worker asked Ms. Murray how was she doing, Ms. Murray stated she was doing well and was ready to go back to work in the next few weeks. Ms. Murray stated multiple times that she was starting to be bored of sitting in the house and would like to go out to work. Ms. Murray asked if worker needed to see the other children in the home, Ms. Murray informed worker that they were in there rooms sleeping. Worker suggested it was best to allow them to sleep. Ms. Murray stated she was ready for the children to go back to school so that things could go back to "normal". Worker asked Ms. Murray if she was in need of any supplies for Joseph such as diapers, wipes, etc. Ms. Murray told worker that she was not in need of anything but appreciated worker asking. Since there seemed to be no concerns or needs, worker concluded the visit. Worker said goodbye to Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe then exited the home. Worker entered the vehicle then exited the premises. </p><p>Makara Griffin, Family Support Worker II. </p>', entitytype='servicecase', entitytypeid='a005cdd3-55ac-4957-96a6-f3db60e87ad1', pagetitle=NULL, pageurl=NULL, islatest=NULL, versionof=NULL, insertedby='5c0a409c-8298-4f81-a7bc-7cc89923ab06', insertedon='2024-12-30 10:48:34.796', archivedby=NULL, archivedon=NULL, updatedby='5c0a409c-8298-4f81-a7b