UPDATE cjams.progressnote
SET progressnotetypeid='786495b2-c779-4cc4-b812-6a8439bfa96e', title=NULL, description='<p>This worker arrived at the home and was greeted by an unknown female, who invited this worker inside. Amber Murray introduced herself and the unknown female as her girlfriend, Julie Hoppe (DOB: 2/5/87). Ms. Murray reports they reside in the apartment together along with her three children. Her two oldest children, Skylar Murray and Makenzie Elliott were at school (Pittsville Elem/Middle Schcool) and don''t usually get home until 330pm.&nbsp; This worker observed Ms. Murrays son, Joseph Murray asleep in her arms. He was dressed in a one-piece outfit and appeared clean and well cared for.&nbsp;</p><p>This worker verified demographic info and Ms. Murray advised her daughter Skylar, DOB: 3/6/11 and Makenzie, DOB: 2/20/15.&nbsp; Ms. Murray advised their father is currently incarcerated and her son Joseph''s father is not involved at all and refused to give a name.&nbsp;</p><p>Before worker discussed the details of Ms. Murray''s case, this worker asked for her permission to speak in front of Ms. Hoppe who was present in the room. Ms. Murray advised Ms. Hoppe was already aware and worker could talk about the case in front of her.</p><p>This worker discussed the reported concerns identified in the SEN referral and asked about her marijuana and cocaine use. Ms. Murray advised that approx. one week before she gave birth, she smoked marijuana with a friend and noticed it made her feel weird. She advised she felt dehydrated, had a vaginal discharge and felt sick so she went to the emergency room to be checked out. She advised it was then that she learned she had ingested cocaine. She denies every using cocaine and only used marijuana. Therefore, she realized that she had smoked marijuana laced with cocaine. She reports not having a medical marijuana card and used marijuana about one time a month for nausea and vomiting. She advised she was sick the entire pregnancy and was prescribed medication for nausea, but it didn''t work for her, so she smoked marijuana. She advised her doctor was aware of her marijuana use.</p><p><span style="color:black;">&nbsp;This worker discussed the risks and concerns of marijuana use in the home and while caring for her son. This worker also discussed the increased risk of SIDS in the event marijuana is used around her son. Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe were both receptive to this info and advised they understood and agreed. Ms. Murray reports no one smokes inside the home and she doesn''t want to put her son or other children in harm''s way. This worker advised her the apartment reeked of what appeared to be cigarette smoke, but Ms. Murray was adamant that no one smokes in the apartment or around the newborn, Joseph. The risks of second hand smoke were also discussed with M.s. Murray and Ms. Hoppe as well as fire safety in the home. Fire escape route was identified. </span>&nbsp;</p><p>Ms. Murray reports no use of any other substances and denied the need for substance abuse treatment at this time. She advised she has not been in substance abuse treatment ever. But she was engaged in mental health services at Comm. Beh. Health a few years ago to treat her Anxiety and Depression. She is not currently prescribed any psychotropic medications and is only taking Prenatal Vitamins, Ibuprofen, and Albuterol inhaler for Asthma. This worker discussed the need for the family to engage in community services and suggested they engage with Birth to Five and Healthy Families. Ms. Murray advised she would think about it but doesn''t feel like they need any additional services. She further advised her son was in mental health as he was diagnosed with ADHD and Depression in the past; approx. 4-5yrs ago. She advised if she finds the need for him to reengage she will put him back in therapy, but he seems to be doing well currently.</p><p>This worker asked Ms. Murray if she experienced any Adverse Childhood Experiences and she advised she was sexually abused as a child but it was previously reported</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Safe sleep was discussed with Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe and they both agreed and advised they understand that Joseph should only sleep in his bassinet, on his back, nothing inside with him and never in bed with them. This worker observed Joseph''s pack n play in the living room and his bassinet next to his mother''s bed. Ms. Murray had an abundance of clothing, diapers, wipes, blankets, and a car seat for Joseph.</p><p>Joseph is feeding 2-3oz of Similac formula about every 2-3hrs and tolerating it well. He was examined at Chesapeake Pediatrics on 12/17/24 and gained weight. His birth weight was 6.5lbs and he weighed 7lbs 5oz at his peds appt.&nbsp; His next pediatric appt. is scheduled for 12/26/24. No issues or concerns noted at the visit and Joseph appeared healthy.</p><p>Ms. Murray is not currently employed and receives $726 in food stamps, $832 TCA, and MA insurance (Priority Partners) for herself and her children. She has a WIC appt. today at 2pm for Joseph. This worker provided her with a Change Form to add Joseph to her benefits and advised her to turn it in asap. Ms. Murray doesn''t have her own transportation and relies on her partner, Julie Hoppe, to transport her. She pays $94 per month to Rent her two-bedroom apartment. This worker advised her that eventually she will have to move to a larger apartment due to her children being different sexes. &nbsp;</p><p>Ms. Murray reports being of Christian faith and attends the 3-C Church sometime and at other times they attend Oak Ridge Baptist Church. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>This worker made Ms. Murray aware that during the first 30 days of the case being opened, weekly home visits will take place to assess the safety of Joseph. She agreed that would be fine as she''s usually at home since she''s currently working.&nbsp; Worker advised she would check in with her periodically, but if she needs anything to call or text this worker''s agency cellphone. &nbsp;</p><p>Worker advised she will need to come back to the home to visit her older two children as all the children in the home must be assessed for safety.&nbsp; Worker also advised Ms. Murray of her leave schedule and advised that a family support worker will visit them in worker''s absence.&nbsp; She advised that would be fine and worker should call or text when they''re enroute. Worker asked Ms. Murray if she has any supports and she identified her partner, Julie and her aunt, Lisa Elliott (telephone #410-726-1110)</p><p>Initial case documents were completed and a Home Health Assessment was completed on the apartment. No health or safety concerns were noted. This worker also requested Ms. Murray complete a urinalysis at Cove Recovery on Monday, Dec. 23rd. She advised she would do so as she has nothing to hide. This worker advised random urinalysis would be requested throughout the duration of the case to ensure she is no longer using cocaine and if she test positive she will need to engage in treatment for further monitoring. Ms. Murray agreed to complete a urinalysis on Monday and worker provided her with the referral form to take with her to the appt.</p><p>Both Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe appeared coherent and not under the influence of marijuana or other substances at this time.</p><p>It should be noted that Ms. Murray and Ms. Hoppe share a cell phone number.</p><p>Kerry Price, MSW</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', entitytype='servicecase', entitytypeid='a005cdd3-55ac-4957-96a6-f3db60e87ad1', pagetitle=NULL, pageurl=NULL, islatest=NULL, versionof=NULL, insertedby='ab7e0e4d-9082-454c-88de-df66a416fcab', insertedon='2024-12-23 01:34:23.995', archivedby=NULL, archivedon=NULL, updatedby='ab7e0e4d-9082-454c-88de-df66a416fcab', updatedon='2024-12-23 01:34:23.995', "timestamp"=NULL, savemode=true, progressnotesubtypeid='f3c40498-cf00-4648-96f0-dbdf562bb6ef', contactdate='2024-12-20 00:00:00.000', contactname=NULL, progressnotetypekey=NULL, contactroletypekey=NULL, contactphone=NULL, contactemail=NULL, attemptindicator=false, activeflag=1, documentpropertiesid=NULL, starttime='2024-12-20 12:40:00.000', endtime='2024-12-20 13:20:00.000', instantresults=1, contactstatus=true, drugscreen=false, progressnotepurposetypekey=NULL, old_id=NULL, traveltime='', totaltime='0:40', progressnotereasontypekey='CM,CMT,IASM,INF,MV,SC,WV', locationname=NULL, witsinboundid=NULL, roletypekey=NULL, islocked=false, stafftypekey='1', notesid=NULL, witsstatus=NULL, witsupdatedate=NULL, witsupdatebyidno=NULL, contactcategoryidno=NULL, iconimgtext=NULL, parametercodeidno=NULL, detaillookup=NULL, fk_id=NULL, initiationindicator=true, intakeserviceid=NULL, servicecaseid='a005cdd3-55ac-4957-96a6-f3db60e87ad1', isintake='N', otherpersonname=NULL, uploadedfile=NULL, adjustmentfostercaretext=NULL, screeningfortheservicetext=NULL, ischildgotoshool=NULL, qualityofcaretochildtext=NULL, fk_user_id=NULL, etl_userid=NULL, etl_load_date=NULL, fromjurisdictionid=NULL, tojurisdictionid=NULL, transferdate=NULL, transfertime=NULL, travelstarttime=NULL, travelendtime=NULL, servicesprovided=NULL, otherservices=NULL, anyriskpresented=NULL, otherrisk=NULL, witsid=14696018, focusperson='{"focuspersonjson":[{"participanttypekey":"IP","intakeservicerequestactorid":"c68026f8-8851-45b3-9259-70b5b4e142b7","participantid":"c68026f8-8851-45b3-9259-70b5b4e142b7","firstname":"JULIA","lastname":"HOPPE","address1":null,"address2":null,"city":null,"state":null,"zipcode":null,"email":null,"phonenumber":null},{"participanttypekey":"IP","intakeservicerequestactorid":"f726b90a-0517-43ad-9fbd-6aca85c1dae7","participantid":"f726b90a-0517-43ad-9fbd-6aca85c1dae7","firstname":"Joseph","lastname":"Murray","address1":null,"address2":null,"city":null,"state":null,"zipcode":null,"email":null,"phonenumber":null}]}', factor1_risk_scale=NULL, factor2_dependent_independent_scale=NULL, factor3_outcome_scale=NULL
WHERE progressnoteid='d988b6f7-69f3-448e-80ab-72ddc3096e06';
UPDATE cjams.progressnote
SET progressnotetypeid='8d25a26b-91a1-4423-947e-e451e8eff6b7', title=NULL, description='<p>This worker spoke with Amber Murray to make her aware of the SEN referral and service case. Ms. Murray advised she was aware that someone would be contacting  her. This worker requested to come out to the home today. Ms. Murray agreed and advised worker to come at any time. This worker advised she would be on her way to the home in the next hour.  </p><p>Kerry Price, MSW </p>', entitytype='servicecase', entitytypeid='a005cdd3-55ac-4957-96a6-f3db60e87ad1', pagetitle=NULL, pageurl=NULL, islatest=NULL, versionof=NULL, insertedby='ab7e0e4d-9082-454c-88de-df66a416fcab', insertedon='2024-12-23 01:30:55.418', archivedby=NULL, archivedon=NULL, updatedby='ab7e0e4d-9082-454c-88de-df66a416fcab', updatedon='2024-12-23 01:38:28.138', "timestamp"=NULL, savemode=true, progressnotesubtypeid='c881fa2c-1450-4c8a-b0c5-e27fb4f707e5', contactdate='2024-12-20 00:00:00.000', contactname=NULL, progressnotetypekey=NULL, contactroletypekey=NULL, contactphone=NULL, contactemail=NULL, attemptindicator=false, activeflag=1, documentpropertiesid=NULL, starttime='2024-12-20 11:24:00.000', endtime='2024-12-20 11:43:00.000', instantresults=1, contactstatus=true, drugscreen=false, progressnotepurposetypekey=NULL, old_id=NULL, traveltime='', totaltime='0:19', progressnotereasontypekey='CM,INF,SCH', locationname='Teleworking ', witsinboundid=NULL, roletypekey=NULL, islocked=false, stafftypekey='1', notesid=NULL, witsstatus=NULL, witsupdatedate=NULL, witsupdatebyidno=NULL, contactcategoryidno=NULL, iconimgtext=NULL, parametercodeidno=NULL, detaillookup=NULL, fk_id=NULL, initiationindicator=true, intakeserviceid=NULL, servicecaseid='a005cdd3-55ac-4957-96a6-f3db60e87ad1', isintake='N', otherpersonname=NULL, uploadedfile=NULL, adjustmentfostercaretext=NULL, screeningfortheservicetext=NULL, ischildgotoshool=NULL, qualityofcaretochildtext=NULL, fk_user_id=NULL, etl_userid=NULL, etl_load_date=NULL, fromjurisdictionid=NU